As explained in Alister Anthony Pereira v. State of Maharashtra (2012) 2 SCC 648, the three things which are required to be proved for an offence under Section 304-A are:
(1) death of human being;
(2) the accused caused the death; and (3) the death was caused by the doing of a rash or negligent act, though it did not amount to culpable homicide of either description.
